codex
Decision: serialize a shallow model copy only when an extra key would collide with a declared field’s actual output key; the copy’s extras omit those colliding keys. This preserves the validated field and avoids mutating the live model. I rejected post-processing because the overwritten value is already lost (and JSON may contain duplicate keys), and rejected temporary mutation because concurrent serialization could observe it.
